foundation.question_text:
The graph shows the number of algae cells $N$ in a sample after $t$ hours.
Write a model for $N$ in the form $N=ka^{t}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.3,xmax=3.7,ymin=-15,ymax=195,xtick={0,1,2,3},ytick={0,20,...,180},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$},ylabel={$N$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,->,domain=0:3.15,samples=100] {20*exp(x*ln(2))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The graph shows the mass $m$ grams of a sample of a chemical after $t$ hours.
Write a model for $m$ in the form $m=ka^{t}$, then use it to find the mass after $5$ hours.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=5.6,ymin=-15,ymax=180,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5},ytick={0,20,...,160},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$},ylabel={$m$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,->,domain=0:5.3,samples=100] {160*exp(x*ln(0.5))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
